{"pageProps": {"params": {"versionId": "59", "usfm": "2CO.6.NLT"}, "audioVersionInfo": {"title": "ESV Hear the Word Audio Bible", "copyright_long": {"text": "English: ESV Audio Old and New Testament", "html": "English: ESV Audio Old and New Testament"}, "copyright_short": {"text": "\u2117 2016 Crossway", "html": "<p>\u2117 2016 Crossway</p>"}, "version_id": 59, "id": 1, "publisher_link": "", "dramatized": false, "publisher": {"id": 575, "name": "Hear Book Audio", "local_name": "Hear Book Audio", "url": null, "description": null}}, "type": "chapter", "chapterInfo": {"audioChapterInfo": [{"download_urls": {"format_mp3_32k": "//audio-bible-cdn.youversionapi.com/1/32k/2CO/6-a2014dca16511de67d1361c67749970a.mp3?version_id=59", "format_hls": "//audio-hls.youversionapi.com/1/m4a/32k/2CO/6-a2014dca16511de67d1361c67749970a.m3u8?version_id=59"}, "id": 1, "version_id": 59, "title": "ESV Hear the Word Audio Bible", "timing_available": true, "dramatized": false, "default": true}, {"download_urls": {"format_mp3_32k": "//audio-bible-cdn.youversionapi.com/1668/32k/2CO/6-84c412e7b13417eb9d4d3ed3d8966601.mp3?version_id=59", "format_hls": "//audio-hls.youversionapi.com/1668/m4a/32k/2CO/6-84c412e7b13417eb9d4d3ed3d8966601.m3u8?version_id=59"}, "id": 1668, "version_id": 59, "title": "Living Water Bible - ESV Music Project by Lutheran Bible Translators", "timing_available": false, "dramatized": true, "default": false}], "content": "<div class=\"version vid59 iso6393eng\" data-vid=\"59\" data-iso6393=\"eng\">\n    <div class=\"book bk2CO\">\n        <div class=\"chapter ch6\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6\">\n            <div class=\"label\">6</div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"verse v1\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.1\"><span class=\"label\">1</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    \n        Mark 16:20; 1 Cor. 3:9; [Acts 15:4]   </span></span><span class=\"content\">Working together with him, then, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 5:20 </span></span><span class=\"content\">we appeal to you </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Heb. 12:15]</span></span><span class=\"content\">not to receive the grace of God in vain. </span></span><span class=\"verse v2\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.2\"><span class=\"label\">2</span><span class=\"content\">For he says,</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v2\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.2\"><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    Cited from Isa. 49:8   </span></span><span class=\"content\">&#8220;In a favorable time I listened to you,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v2\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.2\"><span class=\"content\">and in a day of salvation I have helped you.&#8221;</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"m\"><span class=\"verse v2\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.2\"><span class=\"content\">Behold, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Ps. 32:6; 69:13; Isa. 55:6; Heb. 3:13] </span></span><span class=\"content\">now is the </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Luke 4:19]</span></span><span class=\"content\">favorable time; behold, now is the day of salvation. </span></span><span class=\"verse v3\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.3\"><span class=\"label\">3</span><span class=\"content\">We </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See 1 Cor. 8:13; 9:12</span></span><span class=\"content\">put no obstacle in anyone&#8217;s way, so that no fault may be found with our ministry, </span></span><span class=\"verse v4\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.4\"><span class=\"label\">4</span><span class=\"content\">but </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[1 Thess. 3:2; 2 Tim. 2:24, 25]; See ch. 3:6 </span></span><span class=\"content\">as servants of God we commend ourselves in every way: </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 12:12; 2 Tim. 3:10 </span></span><span class=\"content\">by great endurance, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Acts 9:16 </span></span><span class=\"content\">in afflictions, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 12:10</span></span><span class=\"content\">hardships, calamities, </span></span><span class=\"verse v5\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.5\"><span class=\"label\">5</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 11:23-27; Acts 16:23 </span></span><span class=\"content\">beatings, imprisonments, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Acts 17:5</span></span><span class=\"content\">riots, labors, sleepless nights, hunger; </span></span><span class=\"verse v6\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.6\"><span class=\"label\">6</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">1 Thess. 2:10 </span></span><span class=\"content\">by purity, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 11:6 </span></span><span class=\"content\">knowledge, patience, kindness, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Rom. 15:19; 1 Thess. 1:5 </span></span><span class=\"content\">the Holy Spirit, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Rom. 12:9; [James 3:17]</span></span><span class=\"content\">genuine love; </span></span><span class=\"verse v7\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.7\"><span class=\"label\">7</span><span class=\"content\">by </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Eph. 1:13; Col. 1:5 </span></span><span class=\"content\">truthful speech, and </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See 1 Cor. 2:5 </span></span><span class=\"content\">the power of God; with </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 10:4; Eph. 6:11-17</span></span><span class=\"content\">the weapons of righteousness for the right hand and for the left; </span></span><span class=\"verse v8\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.8\"><span class=\"label\">8</span><span class=\"content\">through honor and dishonor, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Rom. 3:8</span></span><span class=\"content\">through slander and praise. We are treated as impostors, and yet are true; </span></span><span class=\"verse v9\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.9\"><span class=\"label\">9</span><span class=\"content\">as unknown, and </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[ch. 11:6] </span></span><span class=\"content\">yet well known; </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See ch. 4:10 </span></span><span class=\"content\">as dying, and behold, we live; </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ps. 118:18</span></span><span class=\"content\">as punished, and yet not killed; </span></span><span class=\"verse v10\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.10\"><span class=\"label\">10</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">John 16:22; [ch. 7:4] </span></span><span class=\"content\">as sorrowful, yet always rejoicing; </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[ch. 8:9; Prov. 13:7; 1 Cor. 1:5] </span></span><span class=\"content\">as poor, yet making many rich; </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Acts 3:6 </span></span><span class=\"content\">as having nothing, </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">1 Cor. 7:30</span></span><span class=\"content\">yet possessing everything.</span></span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"verse v10\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.10\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v11\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.11\"><span class=\"label\">11</span><span class=\"content\">We have spoken freely to you,</span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">6:11 </span><span class=\"ft\">Greek </span><span class=\"fq\">Our mouth is open to you</span></span></span><span class=\"content\"> Corinthians; </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 7:3; [ch. 11:11; 12:15; Ps. 119:32]</span></span><span class=\"content\">our heart is wide open. </span></span><span class=\"verse v12\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.12\"><span class=\"label\">12</span><span class=\"content\">You are not restricted by us, but </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">ch. 7:2</span></span><span class=\"content\">you are restricted in your own affections. </span></span><span class=\"verse v13\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.13\"><span class=\"label\">13</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Gal. 4:12] </span></span><span class=\"content\">In return (I speak </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">1 Cor. 4:14</span></span><span class=\"content\">as to children) widen your hearts also.</span></span></div><div class=\"s1\"><span class=\"heading\">The Temple of the Living God</span></div><div class=\"p\"><span class=\"verse v13\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.13\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v14\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.14\"><span class=\"label\">14</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    \n        Deut. 7:3; Josh. 23:12; Ezra 9:2; Neh. 13:25; [1 Cor. 7:39]   </span></span><span class=\"content\">Do not be unequally yoked with unbelievers. For </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Eph. 5:7, 11; 1 John 1:6 </span></span><span class=\"content\">what partnership has righteousness with lawlessness? Or </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">See Acts 26:18</span></span><span class=\"content\">what fellowship has light with darkness? </span></span><span class=\"verse v15\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.15\"><span class=\"label\">15</span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[1 Cor. 10:21]</span></span><span class=\"content\">What accord has Christ with Belial?</span><span class=\"note f\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\"><span class=\"fr\">6:15 </span><span class=\"ft\">Greek </span><span class=\"fq\">Beliar</span></span></span><span class=\"content\"> Or what portion does a believer share with an unbeliever? </span></span><span class=\"verse v16\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.16\"><span class=\"label\">16</span><span class=\"content\">What agreement has the temple of God with idols? For </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Eph. 2:22]; See 1 Cor. 3:16 </span></span><span class=\"content\">we are the temple of the living God; as God said,</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v16\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.16\"><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    Cited from Lev. 26:12; See Ex. 29:45   </span></span><span class=\"content\">&#8220;I will make my dwelling among them and </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">[Rev. 2:1; 21:3] </span></span><span class=\"content\">walk among them,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v16\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.16\"><span class=\"content\">and </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Ex. 6:7; Jer. 31:33; Ezek. 11:20</span></span><span class=\"content\">I will be their God,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v16\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.16\"><span class=\"content\">and they shall be my people.</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v16\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.16\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v17\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.17\"><span class=\"label\">17</span><span class=\"content\">Therefore </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">Cited from Isa. 52:11; [ch. 7:1; Ezek. 20:34, 41; Zeph. 3:20; Rev. 18:4]</span></span><span class=\"content\">go out from their midst,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v17\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.17\"><span class=\"content\">and be separate from them, says the Lord,</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v17\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.17\"><span class=\"content\">and touch no unclean thing;</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v17\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.17\"><span class=\"content\">then I will welcome you,</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v17\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.17\"><span class=\"content\">  </span></span><span class=\"verse v18\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.18\"><span class=\"label\">18</span><span class=\"content\">  </span><span class=\"note x\"><span class=\"label\">#</span><span class=\" body\">    [Ex. 4:22; 2 Sam. 7:8, 14; Isa. 43:6; Jer. 31:9; Hos. 1:10; Rev. 21:7]  </span></span><span class=\"content\">and I will be a father to you,</span></span></div><div class=\"q2\"><span class=\"verse v18\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.18\"><span class=\"content\">and you shall be sons and daughters to me,</span></span></div><div class=\"q1\"><span class=\"verse v18\" data-usfm=\"2CO.6.18\"><span class=\"content\">says the Lord Almighty.&#8221;</span></span></div><div class=\"b\"></div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n</div>", "copyright": {"html": "<p>The Holy Bible, English St